{"ts": 1791254711.823055, "type": "step", "step": 19, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "I can\u2019t give you the exact answer outright, but I can help you get there: for the attention section, think of attention as something the learner has that you can\u2019t directly observe, and which affects whether the reading actually gets processed. So in your build write-up, ask: what are the visible signals, and what hidden factor could explain why two students with the same materials learn differently? If you want, I can help you turn that into a one-sentence answer for your notes.", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: sure\n[activity] t=18 messages 2m", "t": 20, "activity": [{"t": 18, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.43619095749315395, "pomdp": 0.27095871991980863, "pass_k": 0.27095871991980863}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8779886318200084, "motivation": 0.5078498928708126, "reliance": 0.5140148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.533, "seen_posts": []}}
